1
00:00:01,543 --> 00:00:02,837
I CAN'T BELIEVE
I'M GETTING MY NAILS DONE.

2
00:00:02,837 --> 00:00:06,131
AND YOU SAID IT WAS
GOING TO BE FUN...

3
00:00:06,131 --> 00:00:08,425
WHICH IT KIND OF IS.

4
00:00:08,425 --> 00:00:10,678
ALSO, YOU SAID
THERE WERE GOING
TO BE OTHER GUYS HERE.

5
00:00:10,678 --> 00:00:12,262
THERE ARE NO
OTHER GUYS HERE.

6
00:00:12,262 --> 00:00:14,389
CHANDLER, THERE'S A GUY
RIGHT OVER THERE.

7
00:00:14,389 --> 00:00:16,934
THAT'S A MAILMAN.

8
00:00:16,934 --> 00:00:19,269
THAT'S OUR MAILMAN.

9
00:00:19,269 --> 00:00:21,229
( mumbling ):
HI. HOW ARE YOU?

10
00:00:25,693 --> 00:00:27,110
CHANDLER, DON'T WORRY.

11
00:00:27,110 --> 00:00:30,155
THIS DOESN'T MAKE YOU
ANY LESS OF A GUY.

12
00:00:30,155 --> 00:00:32,031
THAT DOES.

13
00:00:33,534 --> 00:00:35,744
WHAT AM I SITTING ON?

14
00:00:37,705 --> 00:00:39,874
I'D HATE TO THINK
WHAT THIS WOMAN WAS SCRATCHING

15
00:00:39,874 --> 00:00:41,500
WHEN THIS BROKE OFF.

16
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:43,669
HEY, YOU KNOW
WHO USED TO HAVE
NAILS LIKE THAT?

17
00:00:43,669 --> 00:00:45,086
NO.
Janice:
OH...

18
00:00:45,086 --> 00:00:48,089
MY... GOD.

19
00:00:55,806 --> 00:01:00,811
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

20
00:01:00,811 --> 00:01:03,104
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

21
00:01:03,104 --> 00:01:05,357
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

22
00:01:05,357 --> 00:01:10,362
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

23
00:01:10,362 --> 00:01:12,823
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN YOUR DAY ♪

24
00:01:12,823 --> 00:01:15,910
♪ YOUR WEEK, YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

25
00:01:15,910 --> 00:01:19,454
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

26
00:01:19,454 --> 00:01:21,832
♪ WHEN THE RAIN
STARTS TO POUR ♪

27
00:01:21,832 --> 00:01:24,501
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

28
00:01:24,501 --> 00:01:26,628
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

29
00:01:26,628 --> 00:01:29,423
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

30
00:01:29,423 --> 00:01:34,386
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

31
00:01:40,267 --> 00:01:42,770
JOEY, LET ME
ASK A QUESTION.

32
00:01:42,770 --> 00:01:43,812
THIS HAS BEEN
DRIVING ME CRAZY.

33
00:01:43,812 --> 00:01:45,397
WHAT DOES THIS LIGHT SWITCH DO?

34
00:01:45,397 --> 00:01:46,481
OH, NOTHING.

35
00:01:46,481 --> 00:01:48,025
DIDN'T IT DRIVE YOU CRAZY

36
00:01:48,025 --> 00:01:49,568
NOT TO KNOW WHAT IT DID?

37
00:01:49,568 --> 00:01:51,695
I KNOW WHAT IT DID--
NOTHING.

38
00:01:53,655 --> 00:01:55,783
THEY WOULDN'T HAVE PUT IT THERE
IF IT DIDN'T DO SOMETHING.

39
00:01:55,783 --> 00:01:57,284
HOW CAN YOU NOT CARE?

40
00:01:57,284 --> 00:01:58,243
LIKE THIS.

41
00:02:01,872 --> 00:02:03,624
HERE'S ANOTHER QUESTION
FOR YOU:

42
00:02:03,624 --> 00:02:05,626
DO YOU KNOW WHAT
THAT LITTLE SILVER KNOB

43
00:02:05,626 --> 00:02:06,877
ON THE TOILET DOES?

44
00:02:06,877 --> 00:02:09,296
SURE. IT FLUSHES IT.
OKAY, GOOD.

45
00:02:09,296 --> 00:02:11,339
NOW THAT YOU KNOW,
WHEN YOU COME OVER

46
00:02:11,339 --> 00:02:13,634
WOULD YOU MIND
ACTUALLY USING IT?

47
00:02:15,427 --> 00:02:16,845
HELLO.

48
00:02:16,845 --> 00:02:17,888
HEY.
( yells )

49
00:02:17,888 --> 00:02:19,890
( screams )

50
00:02:19,890 --> 00:02:21,516
OH, MY GOD. WOW.

51
00:02:21,516 --> 00:02:22,935
GUESS WHO WE RAN INTO TODAY.

52
00:02:25,062 --> 00:02:26,229
JANICE.

53
00:02:26,229 --> 00:02:27,230
IS THIS AMAZING?

54
00:02:27,230 --> 00:02:28,983
HOW HAVE YOU BEEN?

55
00:02:28,983 --> 00:02:31,150
WELL, UM...
I'M DIVORCED.

56
00:02:31,150 --> 00:02:33,153
( gasps )
WOW.

57
00:02:33,153 --> 00:02:35,196
YEAH, I'M RIDING
THE ALIMONY PONY.

58
00:02:35,196 --> 00:02:37,365
( machine-gun-fire-
like laughter )

59
00:02:37,365 --> 00:02:40,035
AND THERE IT IS.

60
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:43,080
I JUST CAME UP
TO SAY HI.

61
00:02:43,080 --> 00:02:45,415
HI.
( laughing weakly )

62
00:02:45,415 --> 00:02:47,042
AND YOU, SWEETIE,
I'LL SEE LATER.

63
00:02:47,042 --> 00:02:48,669
OKAY.
I'LL SEE YOU TONIGHT.

64
00:02:48,669 --> 00:02:50,295
OKAY. BYE.
BYE.

65
00:02:50,295 --> 00:02:51,463
BYE. BYE.
BYE. OH, BYE.

66
00:02:51,463 --> 00:02:52,464
BYE-BYE.
BYE-BYE.

67
00:02:52,464 --> 00:02:53,465
BYE. BYE.
OH.

68
00:02:53,465 --> 00:02:55,216
I CAN'T STAND THE WOMAN.

69
00:02:56,969 --> 00:02:58,386
WHAT?

70
00:02:58,386 --> 00:03:00,097
I THOUGHT YOU WERE
CRAZY ABOUT HER.

71
00:03:00,097 --> 00:03:02,307
I KNOW, BUT YOU KNOW
ALL THOSE LITTLE ANNOYING THINGS

72
00:03:02,307 --> 00:03:04,309
THAT SHE DID
BEFORE WE FELL IN LOVE--

73
00:03:04,309 --> 00:03:07,312
LIKE HER VOICE AND HER LAUGH
AND HER PERSONALITY?

74
00:03:07,312 --> 00:03:09,815
THEY'RE ALL BACK
YOU KNOW.

75
00:03:09,815 --> 00:03:12,776
AND SHE'S PICKED UP,
LIKE, NINE NEW ONES.

76
00:03:12,776 --> 00:03:15,821
SO, WHAT ARE YOU DOING
BRINGING HER HERE?
THERE'S PEOPLE HERE.

77
00:03:18,032 --> 00:03:20,325
DON'T WORRY ABOUT IT.
I'M TAKING CARE
OF IT TONIGHT.

78
00:03:20,325 --> 00:03:22,036
YOU ARE NOT.

79
00:03:22,036 --> 00:03:23,704
YOU HAVE NEVER BEEN ABLE
TO BREAK UP WITH HER.

80
00:03:23,704 --> 00:03:25,789
WELL, I DON'T HAVE TO BREAK UP
WITH HER THIS TIME.

81
00:03:25,789 --> 00:03:28,625
WE'RE NOT INVOLVED.
I'M GOING TO DO
A PREEMPTIVE STRIKE.

82
00:03:28,625 --> 00:03:31,837
I'M GOING TO END IT WITH HER
BEFORE IT STARTS.

83
00:03:31,837 --> 00:03:35,632
MY ASS IS, LIKE, FROZEN.

84
00:03:35,632 --> 00:03:38,552
YEAH, TRY STICKING IT
IN THE FREEZER FOR 20 MINUTES.

85
00:03:42,556 --> 00:03:44,516
I'M TELLING YOU.

86
00:03:50,647 --> 00:03:53,650
I CAN'T BELIEVE
YOU REALLY WALK
ALONE HERE AT NIGHT.

87
00:03:53,650 --> 00:03:56,319
I MEAN, YOU HEAR SUCH
STORIES ABOUT NEW YORK.

88
00:03:56,319 --> 00:03:58,321
NO, IT'S REALLY
NOT THAT BAD.

89
00:03:58,321 --> 00:04:00,407
I MEAN, I-I FOR ONE
FEEL PERFECTLY SAFE.

90
00:04:00,407 --> 00:04:01,408
Men:
EM! EM!

91
00:04:01,408 --> 00:04:02,868
( laughing )

92
00:04:02,868 --> 00:04:04,078
HELP! HELP!

93
00:04:04,078 --> 00:04:05,079
HELP!

94
00:04:05,079 --> 00:04:06,621
COME HERE, LOVE.

95
00:04:06,621 --> 00:04:07,998
NO-NO-NO, ROSS.

96
00:04:07,998 --> 00:04:10,000
ROSS, THESE ARE FRIENDS OF MINE
FROM HOME.

97
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,334
LIAM, DEVON...

98
00:04:11,334 --> 00:04:12,335
THIS IS ROSS.

99
00:04:12,335 --> 00:04:13,587
OH.
HI, MATE.

100
00:04:13,587 --> 00:04:15,130
HEY.
HOW ARE YOU, MATE?

101
00:04:15,130 --> 00:04:17,382
HA!
THAT WAS A GOOD ONE, HUH?

102
00:04:17,382 --> 00:04:19,467
"HELP! HELP!"

103
00:04:19,467 --> 00:04:21,178
Emily:
SO, HOW ARE YOU?

104
00:04:21,178 --> 00:04:23,638
I'VE BEEN MEANING TO RING
YOU EVER SINCE I ARRIVED

105
00:04:23,638 --> 00:04:26,767
BUT, UM, WELL, I'VE
BEEN RATHER BUSY.

106
00:04:26,767 --> 00:04:30,145
DO YOU REALIZE WE HAVE NOT SEEN
EACH OTHER SINCE THE NIGHT
OF THAT U2 CONCERT?

107
00:04:30,145 --> 00:04:32,522
HUH.
OH, MY GOD, I THINK
YOU'RE RIGHT.

108
00:04:32,522 --> 00:04:34,149
WELL, ACTUALLY,
THE LAST TIME

109
00:04:34,149 --> 00:04:36,568
YOU AND I SAW EACH OTHER
WAS THE NEXT MORNING.

110
00:04:36,568 --> 00:04:38,445
( chuckling ):
OH, LIAM.

111
00:04:38,445 --> 00:04:40,864
HA! OH, LIAM.

112
00:04:42,950 --> 00:04:45,244
SO, UH, WHAT, WERE YOU GUYS
PLAYING SOCCER OR SOME...?

113
00:04:45,244 --> 00:04:49,248
( with fake British accent):
OR-OR SHOULD I CALL IT
FOOTBALL?

114
00:04:49,248 --> 00:04:51,332
WE WERE PLAYING RUGBY.

115
00:04:51,332 --> 00:04:53,334
WE'RE PLAYING A GAME
AT THE PARK TOMORROW.

116
00:04:53,334 --> 00:04:54,920
YOU'RE WELCOME TO PLAY, TOO,
IF YOU WANT.

117
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:56,255
ROSS PLAY RUGBY?

118
00:04:56,255 --> 00:04:57,589
I DON'T THINK SO.

119
00:04:57,589 --> 00:04:59,258
( mirthless chuckle )

120
00:04:59,258 --> 00:05:02,136
WHAT... WHAT'S SO FUNNY
ABOUT THAT?

121
00:05:02,136 --> 00:05:03,386
WELL, I MEAN...

122
00:05:03,386 --> 00:05:05,346
YOU'RE AMERICAN
TO START WITH.

123
00:05:05,346 --> 00:05:07,808
YOU DON'T REALLY
HAVE RUGBY HERE.

124
00:05:07,808 --> 00:05:09,893
WELL, WE DIDN'T
HAVE FREEDOM HERE

125
00:05:09,893 --> 00:05:12,771
UNTIL 1776 EITHER, SO...

126
00:05:12,771 --> 00:05:14,313
SO, GOOD, THEN.
WE'LL SEE YOU

127
00:05:14,313 --> 00:05:15,732
AT RIVERSIDE
PARK AT 2:00.

128
00:05:15,732 --> 00:05:17,192
CHEERS.
CHEERS.
CHEERS.

129
00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:19,861
( grunting )

130
00:05:19,861 --> 00:05:21,488
( grunting )

131
00:05:26,243 --> 00:05:30,371
OH, BOY, I JUST
LOVE TO SING.

132
00:05:30,371 --> 00:05:31,915
YES, I-I KNOW
THAT YOU DO.

133
00:05:31,915 --> 00:05:34,209
I THINK ONE OF THE REASONS
PEOPLE WERE COMPLAINING

134
00:05:34,209 --> 00:05:35,836
WAS BECAUSE
MOST OF THE PEOPLE HAD PAID

135
00:05:35,836 --> 00:05:38,922
TO HEAR THE ACTOR 
SING "OLD MAN RIVER."

136
00:05:38,922 --> 00:05:41,091
OH, LOOK AT US.
WHO WOULD HAVE THOUGHT

137
00:05:41,091 --> 00:05:43,885
THAT CUPID HAD A STATION
AT 14th STREET NAILS?

138
00:05:43,885 --> 00:05:46,429
( machine-gun-fire-
like laughter )

139
00:05:46,429 --> 00:05:49,557
OKAY, WE HAVE TO TALK.

140
00:05:49,557 --> 00:05:53,687
I'M JUST GETTING OUT
OF A VERY SERIOUS RELATIONSHIP.

141
00:05:53,687 --> 00:05:55,147
I KNOW...

142
00:05:55,147 --> 00:05:57,149
AND I'M JUST GETTING
OUT OF A MARRIAGE.

143
00:05:57,149 --> 00:06:00,777
I MEAN, TALK ABOUT
"MEANT TO BE."

144
00:06:00,777 --> 00:06:02,279
RIGHT...

145
00:06:02,279 --> 00:06:04,447
BUT I JUST THINK
THIS IS HAPPENING TOO SOON.

146
00:06:04,447 --> 00:06:07,784
OH, TOO SOON,
TOO SCHMOON.

147
00:06:07,784 --> 00:06:11,454
FACE IT, HONEY--
I AM NOT LETTING YOU
GET AWAY THIS TIME.

148
00:06:11,454 --> 00:06:12,998
I HEAR YOU...

149
00:06:12,998 --> 00:06:14,291
( chuckling )

150
00:06:16,793 --> 00:06:18,128
BUT...

151
00:06:18,128 --> 00:06:21,298
UNFORTUNATELY,
MY COMPANY...

152
00:06:21,298 --> 00:06:23,591
IS TRANSFERRING
ME OVERSEAS.

153
00:06:25,927 --> 00:06:27,971
OH, NO.

154
00:06:27,971 --> 00:06:30,098
WHERE TO?

155
00:06:30,098 --> 00:06:32,100
( gasping ):
TO PARIS?
NO.

156
00:06:32,100 --> 00:06:33,768
NO, NOT-NOT PARIS.

157
00:06:33,768 --> 00:06:35,896
TO LONDON?
OH, NO. ROME?

158
00:06:35,896 --> 00:06:37,898
VIENNA?
OH, OOH, BARCELONA?

159
00:06:37,898 --> 00:06:40,901
OKAY, COULD YOU JUST
STOP TALKING FOR A SECOND?

160
00:06:43,153 --> 00:06:44,154
YEMEN.

161
00:06:44,154 --> 00:06:45,446
( gasping )

162
00:06:46,740 --> 00:06:48,200
THAT'S RIGHT, YES.

163
00:06:48,200 --> 00:06:50,702
I'M BEING TRANSFERRED
TO YEMEN.

164
00:06:50,702 --> 00:06:52,037
WHEN?

165
00:06:52,037 --> 00:06:53,914
I DON'T KNOW EXACTLY...

166
00:06:53,914 --> 00:06:55,165
OH.

167
00:06:55,165 --> 00:06:58,543
WELL, I WILL
JUST HAVE TO SOAK UP

168
00:06:58,543 --> 00:07:01,129
EVERY OUNCE OF CHANDLER BING

169
00:07:01,129 --> 00:07:05,300
UNTIL THAT MOMENT COMES.

170
00:07:05,300 --> 00:07:07,594
BUT I DO KNOW IT'S
SOMETIME TOMORROW.

171
00:07:11,932 --> 00:07:13,308
DONE?

172
00:07:13,308 --> 00:07:14,309
YEP.

173
00:07:14,309 --> 00:07:15,310
HEY.

174
00:07:15,310 --> 00:07:16,311
HEY.
HEY.

175
00:07:16,311 --> 00:07:17,812
WHAT'S UP?

176
00:07:17,812 --> 00:07:19,689
THIS SWITCH THING
HAS BEEN DRIVING ME CRAZY.

177
00:07:19,689 --> 00:07:22,150
SO I TURNED IT OFF
AND CHECKED EVERY OUTLET.

178
00:07:22,150 --> 00:07:24,945
FOUR DON'T WORK,
WHICH MEANS ONE OF THEM

179
00:07:24,945 --> 00:07:26,405
HAS TO BE CONTROLLED
BY THE SWITCH.

180
00:07:26,405 --> 00:07:28,156
SO, I PLUGGED
IN THINGS

181
00:07:28,156 --> 00:07:30,450
IN ALL FOUR OUTLETS
THAT MAKE NOISE.

182
00:07:30,450 --> 00:07:32,660
THAT WAY, WHEN I TURN IT ON
I JUST FOLLOW THE NOISE

183
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:35,289
AND FIND OUT
WHICH ONE IT IS.

184
00:07:35,289 --> 00:07:37,540
I BET I STOPPED LISTENING
BEFORE YOU DID.

185
00:07:39,167 --> 00:07:42,003
YOU KNOW, YOU-YOU ALSO COULD
HAVE USED, UH, LAMPS

186
00:07:42,003 --> 00:07:44,005
AND THEN FOLLOWED THE LIGHT.

187
00:07:44,005 --> 00:07:47,384
YEAH, WELL,
I'M USING NOISE.

188
00:07:47,384 --> 00:07:49,010
ALL RIGHT.
OKAY.

189
00:07:49,010 --> 00:07:50,637
ALL RIGHT. SO,
EVERYBODY READY?

190
00:07:50,637 --> 00:07:52,139
OKAY.
Monica:
HERE WE GO.

191
00:07:53,890 --> 00:07:55,725
( low-pitched humming )

192
00:07:55,725 --> 00:07:57,727
I HEAR SOMETHING.
I HEAR SOMETHING.

193
00:07:57,727 --> 00:07:59,187
WHERE IS IT?

194
00:08:01,273 --> 00:08:03,275
( pitch rising )

195
00:08:03,275 --> 00:08:04,901
( humming )

196
00:08:10,115 --> 00:08:11,950
IT'S COMING FROM JOEY.

197
00:08:11,950 --> 00:08:13,410
( humming continues )

198
00:08:13,410 --> 00:08:15,245
OH, MY GOD,
THAT'S SO FREAKY.

199
00:08:15,245 --> 00:08:16,746
TURN HIM OFF!

200
00:08:19,624 --> 00:08:21,960
Sportscaster:
Goes back to England
with the set scrum

201
00:08:21,960 --> 00:08:23,711
in center field
inside to Hall.

202
00:08:23,711 --> 00:08:24,712
OOH, HEY.

203
00:08:24,712 --> 00:08:25,713
Rachel:
HI.

204
00:08:25,713 --> 00:08:27,132
CAN WE PUT ON THE NEWS?

205
00:08:27,132 --> 00:08:29,343
I THINK
IT MIGHT BE RAINING.

206
00:08:29,343 --> 00:08:30,802
NO. JUST HOLD
ON A SEC.

207
00:08:30,802 --> 00:08:33,554
I'M WATCHING THIS
RUGBY THING ON ESPN.

208
00:08:33,554 --> 00:08:34,973
I DON'T KNOW WHAT
THE BIG DEAL IS.

209
00:08:34,973 --> 00:08:37,100
I'M MAN ENOUGH TO
PLAY THIS SPORT.

210
00:08:37,100 --> 00:08:38,477
DUDE, YOU'RE
NOT EVEN MAN ENOUGH

211
00:08:38,477 --> 00:08:41,021
TO ORDER THE CHANNEL
THAT CARRIES THE SPORT.

212
00:08:42,481 --> 00:08:45,484
HEY THERE, ROSS.

213
00:08:45,484 --> 00:08:46,485
HEY.

214
00:08:46,485 --> 00:08:47,486
JANICE.

215
00:08:49,196 --> 00:08:50,613
( door closing )

216
00:08:50,613 --> 00:08:52,199
YOU KNOW, UH...

217
00:08:52,199 --> 00:08:54,409
YOU REALLY DIDN'T HAVE
TO HELP ME PACK.

218
00:08:54,409 --> 00:08:57,329
WHEN YOU SAID ALL YOU WERE
GOING TO BE DOING BETWEEN NOW

219
00:08:57,329 --> 00:08:58,997
AND THE TIME YOU LEAVE
IS PACKING

220
00:08:58,997 --> 00:09:01,416
YOU REALLY DIDN'T LEAVE ME
MUCH CHOICE, DID YOU?

221
00:09:01,416 --> 00:09:04,127
WELL, I THOUGHT I DID,
BUT I-I GUESS I DID NOT.

222
00:09:05,586 --> 00:09:06,587
HEY.

223
00:09:06,587 --> 00:09:07,797
WHAT'S GOING ON?

224
00:09:07,797 --> 00:09:08,840
OH, I'M PACKING.

225
00:09:08,840 --> 00:09:10,342
YOU KNOW, I-I'M PACKING

226
00:09:10,342 --> 00:09:12,552
'CAUSE I'M MOVING
TO YEMEN TOMORROW.

227
00:09:12,552 --> 00:09:15,055
WELL, THANKS FOR TELLING ME.

228
00:09:17,849 --> 00:09:20,268
I'M ONLY PRETEND
MOVING TO YEMEN, OKAY?

229
00:09:20,268 --> 00:09:22,229
IT'S THE ONLY WAY I
CAN GET RID OF HER.

230
00:09:22,229 --> 00:09:24,022
OH... GOOD ONE.

231
00:09:24,022 --> 00:09:26,024
YEAH...
AND YEMEN.

232
00:09:26,024 --> 00:09:27,650
THAT ACTUALLY SOUNDS
LIKE A REAL COUNTRY.

233
00:09:29,361 --> 00:09:31,821
HEY, CHANDLER, COME ON.
I'LL SHOW YOU

234
00:09:31,821 --> 00:09:34,074
HOW TO ROLL UP YOUR UNDERWEAR
AND STUFF IT IN YOUR SHOES.

235
00:09:34,074 --> 00:09:35,742
IT'S A REAL SPACE SAVER.

236
00:09:35,742 --> 00:09:38,703
YEAH, I KNOW. I DO THAT
'CAUSE IT MAKES ME LOOK TALLER.

237
00:09:40,247 --> 00:09:41,664
Janice:
OKAY, CHANDLER.

238
00:09:41,664 --> 00:09:43,208
COME ON.

239
00:09:43,208 --> 00:09:44,501
OKAY.

240
00:09:44,501 --> 00:09:47,212
JOEY, TRADE LIVES WITH ME.
NOPE.

241
00:09:48,963 --> 00:09:50,924
MAN, LOOK AT THIS.
I CAN'T BELIEVE

242
00:09:50,924 --> 00:09:52,175
YOU SAID
YOU'D PLAY RUGBY.

243
00:09:52,175 --> 00:09:53,468
LOOK HOW BRUTAL
THIS IS.

244
00:09:53,468 --> 00:09:54,969
HEY, I CAN HANDLE IT.

245
00:09:54,969 --> 00:09:56,513
OH, PLEASE, ROSS.

246
00:09:56,513 --> 00:10:00,434
YOU-YOU GOT HURT PLAYING
BADMINTON WITH MY DAD.

247
00:10:00,434 --> 00:10:04,062
THAT'S 'CAUSE YOUR MOM'S DOG
KEPT-KEPT LOOKING AT ME.

248
00:10:05,688 --> 00:10:07,524
OKAY, ROSS
LOOK-LOOK-LOOK-LOOK.

249
00:10:07,524 --> 00:10:09,401
RIGHT HERE, IT'S
CALLED A SCRUM, OKAY?

250
00:10:09,401 --> 00:10:10,735
IT'S KIND OF
LIKE A HUDDLE.

251
00:10:10,735 --> 00:10:13,530
AND IS A HUM
KIND OF LIKE A SCRUDDLE?

252
00:10:13,530 --> 00:10:14,613
( chuckling )

253
00:10:14,613 --> 00:10:15,782
ROSS...

254
00:10:15,782 --> 00:10:17,242
THEY'RE GOING
TO KILL YOU.

255
00:10:19,202 --> 00:10:21,079
NOW, WHY ARE YOU
DOING THIS ANYWAY?

256
00:10:21,079 --> 00:10:23,081
WELL, YOU SHOULD
HAVE SEEN THE GUY

257
00:10:23,081 --> 00:10:24,791
THAT SHE USED
TO GO OUT WITH.

258
00:10:24,791 --> 00:10:27,127
I MEAN, HE'S LIKE...
JOE RUGBY.

259
00:10:27,127 --> 00:10:29,463
YOU'RE KIDDING...
AND HE PLAYS RUGBY?

260
00:10:29,463 --> 00:10:30,547
THAT'S SO FUNNY.

261
00:10:30,547 --> 00:10:32,006
( laughing )

262
00:10:32,006 --> 00:10:33,091
OH, I SEE.

263
00:10:33,091 --> 00:10:34,717
YOU DID THAT. ALL RIGHT.

264
00:10:34,717 --> 00:10:36,344
( sighs )

265
00:10:36,344 --> 00:10:38,930
ANYWAY, SHE THOUGHT
THE VERY IDEA OF ME

266
00:10:38,930 --> 00:10:40,807
PLAYING RUGBY WITH HIM
WAS, LIKE, HILARIOUS.

267
00:10:40,807 --> 00:10:43,435
SO, I'M GOING TO SHOW HER
HOW TOUGH I REALLY AM.

268
00:10:43,435 --> 00:10:44,894
( snickering )

269
00:10:46,271 --> 00:10:47,772
I'M SORRY. YOU'RE RIGHT.

270
00:10:47,772 --> 00:10:49,357
YOU ARE A TOUGH GUY.

271
00:10:49,357 --> 00:10:51,776
YOU ARE THE TOUGHEST
PALEONTOLOGIST I KNOW.

272
00:10:51,776 --> 00:10:53,278
ALL RIGHT, COME ON.

273
00:10:53,278 --> 00:10:55,280
LOOK, ROSS COULD
TAKE CARE OF HIMSELF.

274
00:10:55,280 --> 00:10:56,948
IT'S NOT LIKE
HE'S CHANDLER.

275
00:10:56,948 --> 00:10:58,783
Chandler:
THANKS.

276
00:10:58,783 --> 00:11:00,910
LOOK, DON'T WORRY
ABOUT ME, OKAY?

277
00:11:00,910 --> 00:11:02,621
I'LL JUST LOOK
REAL ENERGETIC

278
00:11:02,621 --> 00:11:04,581
AND STAY AWAY
FROM THE BALL.

279
00:11:04,581 --> 00:11:07,334
I'LL BE THAT GUY
RIGHT OUTSIDE THE CIRCLE.

280
00:11:07,334 --> 00:11:08,918
Ojomo to Back to Bracken.

281
00:11:08,918 --> 00:11:09,919
OH!

282
00:11:09,919 --> 00:11:12,671
OH!
OH, GEEZ.

283
00:11:12,671 --> 00:11:15,342
OH. WELL, MAYBE
THERE WAS A DOG LOOKING AT HIM.

284
00:11:24,767 --> 00:11:26,353
Joey:
OH, HEY,
ROSS, ROSS, ROSS.

285
00:11:26,353 --> 00:11:28,605
YOU WANT TO STAY AWAY
FROM THAT GUY
AND THAT GUY

286
00:11:28,605 --> 00:11:29,897
AND THAT ONE.

287
00:11:29,897 --> 00:11:32,942
DUDE, THEY'RE
ALL HUGE.

288
00:11:32,942 --> 00:11:34,944
THEY DON'T LOOK
ANY BIGGER THAN ME.

289
00:11:34,944 --> 00:11:36,946
WELL, MAYBE THAT'S 'CAUSE
YOU'RE CLOSER TO YOU

290
00:11:36,946 --> 00:11:40,325
SO YOU LOOK BIGGER TO
YOU FROM WHERE YOU ARE.

291
00:11:40,325 --> 00:11:43,161
I'M JUST GOING TO GO
AND SAY "HELLO" TO
THE LADS, ALL RIGHT?

292
00:11:43,161 --> 00:11:44,745
ALL RIGHT.
OKAY.

293
00:11:47,706 --> 00:11:49,543
HI.

294
00:11:49,543 --> 00:11:50,793
OH.

295
00:11:51,878 --> 00:11:53,505
I KIND OF LIKED IT.

296
00:11:53,505 --> 00:11:55,674
( whistle blows )

297
00:11:55,674 --> 00:11:57,467
OKAY. I KNOW WHAT
I'VE GOT TO DO.

298
00:11:57,467 --> 00:11:59,177
I'VE GOT TO GO "RED ROSS."

299
00:12:00,845 --> 00:12:03,848
YOU KNOW, "RED ROSS"?

300
00:12:03,848 --> 00:12:05,642
TOTALLY DON'T KNOW
WHAT YOU'RE TALKING ABOUT.

301
00:12:05,642 --> 00:12:08,019
COME ON, THE TIME THAT WE
WERE ALL WAITING IN LINE

302
00:12:08,019 --> 00:12:09,812
FOR DANCES WITH WOLVES 
AND THAT ONE GUY

303
00:12:09,812 --> 00:12:12,731
CUT IN FRONT OF US
AND I-I JUST LOST IT?

304
00:12:12,731 --> 00:12:15,943
HUH? SCREAMED AT HIM,
TURNED ALL RED?

305
00:12:15,943 --> 00:12:17,487
"RED ROSS"!

306
00:12:19,072 --> 00:12:20,240
NO.

307
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:21,366
YOU'LL SEE.

308
00:12:23,493 --> 00:12:25,744
LIAM, DO ME A FAVOR.
YEAH?

309
00:12:25,744 --> 00:12:27,539
TELL THE LADS
TO GO EASY ON ROSS.

310
00:12:27,539 --> 00:12:28,789
IT'S HIS FIRST TIME.

311
00:12:28,789 --> 00:12:30,667
YOU DON'T SAY.

312
00:12:36,464 --> 00:12:37,756
THANK YOU.

313
00:12:37,756 --> 00:12:39,926
OKAY.

314
00:12:39,926 --> 00:12:41,760
GOOD LUCK, BABE.

315
00:12:41,760 --> 00:12:42,761
Liam:
ROSS!

316
00:12:42,761 --> 00:12:44,556
ROSS, COME ON!
GET IN HERE!

317
00:12:44,556 --> 00:12:46,057
( players shouting )

318
00:12:46,057 --> 00:12:47,267
Liam:
ROSS, COME ON.

319
00:12:50,978 --> 00:12:52,897
( player growls )

320
00:12:52,897 --> 00:12:54,065
COME ON...

321
00:12:54,065 --> 00:12:55,066
ROSS!

322
00:12:55,066 --> 00:12:56,526
ROSS, COME ON.

323
00:12:56,526 --> 00:12:57,818
GET IN THE
BLOODY SCRUM.

324
00:12:57,818 --> 00:12:59,320
Devon:
ROSS, GET IN!

325
00:13:01,615 --> 00:13:03,617
( Ross yelling )

326
00:13:03,617 --> 00:13:04,951
HELP! HELP!

327
00:13:04,951 --> 00:13:06,869
HELP! HELP! HELP!

328
00:13:06,869 --> 00:13:09,080
HELP! HELP! HELP!

329
00:13:10,957 --> 00:13:12,875
SOMEBODY!

330
00:13:15,462 --> 00:13:18,214
OH! YOU... ARE... NOT
GOING TO BELIEVE IT.

331
00:13:18,214 --> 00:13:20,049
JOSHUA CAME INTO WORK TODAY,
AND GUESS WHAT HAPPENED?

332
00:13:20,049 --> 00:13:21,884
HE ASKED YOU OUT?
NO.

333
00:13:21,884 --> 00:13:23,886
BUT I WAS SHOWING
HIM SOME CUFF LINKS

334
00:13:23,886 --> 00:13:25,722
AND I FELT HIS PULSE.

335
00:13:27,474 --> 00:13:28,433
SAUCY.

336
00:13:30,435 --> 00:13:31,936
WHAT ARE THESE?
AH.

337
00:13:31,936 --> 00:13:34,897
ELECTRICAL PLANS
FOR THE BUILDING.

338
00:13:34,897 --> 00:13:37,108
OKAY, OKAY, OKAY.
SHOULD I BE SCARED?

339
00:13:38,568 --> 00:13:40,570
I KNOW THAT SWITCH HAS GOT
TO DO SOMETHING, OKAY?

340
00:13:40,570 --> 00:13:42,572
SO-SO I WENT
DOWN TO CITY HALL
AND I GOT THESE.

341
00:13:42,572 --> 00:13:44,157
ALL I HAD TO DO
IS PAY $25

342
00:13:44,157 --> 00:13:46,660
AND WAIT IN LINE
FOR THREE HOURS.

343
00:13:46,660 --> 00:13:48,911
WOW! IF ONLY MORE PEOPLE KNEW.

344
00:14:01,424 --> 00:14:04,719
YOU KNOW, YOU REALLY DIDN'T
HAVE TO TAKE ME TO THE AIRPORT.

345
00:14:04,719 --> 00:14:08,014
OH, PLEASE. EVERY
MOMENT IS PRECIOUS.

346
00:14:08,014 --> 00:14:11,601
BESIDES, SOMEBODY HAD TO RIDE
IN THAT OTHER TAXI WITH
THE REST OF YOUR LUGGAGE

347
00:14:11,601 --> 00:14:14,729
AND YOUR FRIENDS DON'T
SEEM TO CARE VERY MUCH
THAT YOU'RE LEAVING.

348
00:14:14,729 --> 00:14:17,106
WELL, WE'RE NOT
REALLY THAT CLOSE.

349
00:14:18,775 --> 00:14:21,068
OKAY, SO, I GUESS
THIS IS, UH...

350
00:14:21,068 --> 00:14:22,445
YOU KNOW, GOOD-BYE, THEN.

351
00:14:22,445 --> 00:14:24,823
OH, NO! NO,
IT'S NOT GOOD-BYE.

352
00:14:24,823 --> 00:14:28,451
I'M NOT LEAVING UNTIL
YOU GET ON THAT PLANE.

353
00:14:28,451 --> 00:14:31,830
OKAY, WELL, I GUESS
JUST WAIT HERE, THEN.

354
00:14:34,081 --> 00:14:38,545
HI. I NEED A FAKE
TICKET TO YEMEN.

355
00:14:38,545 --> 00:14:40,921
ONE TICKET TO YEMEN?
OH, NO, NO.
NO, NO, NO, NO.

356
00:14:40,921 --> 00:14:43,591
I JUST NEED... I JUST
NEED A PRETEND TICKET.

357
00:14:43,591 --> 00:14:45,844
I-I'M SORRY, SIR.
I DON'T UNDERSTAND.

358
00:14:45,844 --> 00:14:49,013
WHAT WOULD YOU GIVE A KID
IF HE WANTED A TICKET
TO PLAY WITH?

359
00:14:49,013 --> 00:14:50,724
ARE YOU TRAVELING
WITH A CHILD?

360
00:14:52,767 --> 00:14:55,186
NO.

361
00:14:55,186 --> 00:14:57,021
ALL RIGHT, LOOK,
YOU KNOW WHAT?

362
00:14:57,021 --> 00:14:59,106
SHE'S GOING TO THINK
THAT I'M HANDING
YOU A CREDIT CARD

363
00:14:59,106 --> 00:15:02,943
BUT WHAT I'M
REALLY GOING TO DO
IS HAND YOU A LIBRARY CARD.

364
00:15:02,943 --> 00:15:07,031
UH... SIR, A TICKET
TO YEMEN IS $2,100

365
00:15:07,031 --> 00:15:09,033
AND WE DON'T TAKE
LIBRARY CARDS.

366
00:15:09,033 --> 00:15:12,078
WHAT'S THE MATTER?
IS SOMETHING WRONG?

367
00:15:12,078 --> 00:15:14,163
( gasps )
DO YOU HAVE TO STAY?

368
00:15:15,665 --> 00:15:16,833
AMERICAN EXPRESS?

369
00:15:21,755 --> 00:15:22,714
ROSS!

370
00:15:27,093 --> 00:15:28,469
OH!
I CAN'T BELIEVE

371
00:15:28,469 --> 00:15:29,679
THEY'RE DOING
THAT TO HIM.

372
00:15:29,679 --> 00:15:31,681
I TOLD THEM TO
GO EASY ON HIM.

373
00:15:31,681 --> 00:15:34,517
NO OFFENSE, BUT, YOU KNOW
SOMETIMES IT'S HARD
TO UNDERSTAND YOU

374
00:15:34,517 --> 00:15:36,561
YOU KNOW,
WITH THE ACCENT, SO...

375
00:15:36,561 --> 00:15:38,145
( blows whistle )

376
00:15:38,145 --> 00:15:40,648
THAT'S JUST HALFTIME.
THERE'S MORE OF THIS.

377
00:15:40,648 --> 00:15:41,649
Joey:
OH, HEY.

378
00:15:41,649 --> 00:15:42,983
Phoebe:
HEY.

379
00:15:42,983 --> 00:15:44,485
( panting ):
DID YOU SEE ME?

380
00:15:44,485 --> 00:15:45,820
I WAS PRETTY GOOD, HUH?

381
00:15:45,820 --> 00:15:48,072
THAT IS ONE FUN GAME.

382
00:15:48,072 --> 00:15:49,657
RIGHT.
HEY, DO ME
A FAVOR.

383
00:15:49,657 --> 00:15:52,911
COULD YOU JUST GRAB ME
A BOTTLE OF WATER? THANKS.

384
00:15:52,911 --> 00:15:54,328
( gasps )

385
00:15:54,328 --> 00:15:55,705
I-I THINK I'M DYING.

386
00:15:55,705 --> 00:15:56,706
I-I REALLY DO.

387
00:15:56,706 --> 00:15:57,998
OH, YOU POOR BABY...

388
00:15:57,998 --> 00:16:00,000
TELL MY SON
THAT I LOVE HIM.

389
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:01,294
OKAY.

390
00:16:01,294 --> 00:16:02,796
OH, EXCELLENT.

391
00:16:02,796 --> 00:16:04,798
OH, OKAY, GOT TO
HAVE SOME MORE FUN.

392
00:16:04,798 --> 00:16:06,674
ROSS, THEY ARE
KILLING YOU OUT THERE.

393
00:16:06,674 --> 00:16:08,259
MM-MMM.

394
00:16:08,259 --> 00:16:09,385
THAT'S NOT TRUE.

395
00:16:09,385 --> 00:16:11,471
SHE'S RIGHT.
YOU HAVE TO STOP.

396
00:16:11,471 --> 00:16:13,347
WHAT? NO. NO,
I'M NOT STOPPING.

397
00:16:13,347 --> 00:16:14,766
I'M "RED ROSS."

398
00:16:14,766 --> 00:16:16,183
DUDE, YOU GO
BACK OUT THERE

399
00:16:16,183 --> 00:16:18,185
YOU'RE GOING
TO BE DEAD ROSS.

400
00:16:18,185 --> 00:16:19,854
I DON'T CARE.
I AM NOT QUITTING.

401
00:16:19,854 --> 00:16:21,564
I AM GOING
TO FINISH THIS GAME.

402
00:16:21,564 --> 00:16:23,190
IF YOU INSIST
ON DOING THIS

403
00:16:23,190 --> 00:16:24,734
AT LEAST LET ME
HELP YOU.

404
00:16:24,734 --> 00:16:27,069
NO. GOD, NO. THAT IS
NO PLACE FOR A WOMAN.

405
00:16:27,069 --> 00:16:28,947
THOSE GUYS WILL
GRAB ANYTHING.

406
00:16:28,947 --> 00:16:31,031
NO, THAT'S NOT
WHAT I WAS SAYING.

407
00:16:31,031 --> 00:16:32,700
I JUST MIGHT KNOW
A FEW THINGS

408
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:34,786
THAT COULD HELP YOU 
INFLICT SOME PAIN.

409
00:16:34,786 --> 00:16:36,537
I LIKE THAT.
YEAH?

410
00:16:36,537 --> 00:16:40,541
LISTEN CLOSELY:
DEVON HAS GOT A WEAK ANKLE.
HUH?

411
00:16:40,541 --> 00:16:42,877
ONE SWIFT KICK,
AND HE'LL BACK OFF.

412
00:16:42,877 --> 00:16:44,838
BAD ANKLE. GOT IT!

413
00:16:44,838 --> 00:16:47,006
AND THAT BIG BLOKE
WITH THE BEARD...
UH-HUH?

414
00:16:47,006 --> 00:16:49,007
HE'S GOT A TRICK HIP.
HUH-HA!

415
00:16:49,007 --> 00:16:51,135
YEAH. AND DAVID
OVER THERE

416
00:16:51,135 --> 00:16:52,762
I'VE HEARD THAT
HE DOESN'T WEAR A CUP.

417
00:16:52,762 --> 00:16:54,054
WELL, I COULD USE THAT.

418
00:16:54,054 --> 00:16:56,390
TRICK HIP, NO CUP.
OKAY, OKAY!

419
00:16:56,390 --> 00:16:59,185
AND-AND LIAM--
LIAM'S GOT BAD KNEES.

420
00:16:59,185 --> 00:17:01,354
YOU HIT HIM RIGHT
AND HE'LL GO DOWN
LIKE A LAMP.

421
00:17:01,354 --> 00:17:03,272
BUT-BUT LIAM'S
ON MY TEAM.

422
00:17:03,272 --> 00:17:04,816
I DON'T CARE.
YOU JUST GET THEM!

423
00:17:04,816 --> 00:17:06,442
I'M GOING TO GET HIM!

424
00:17:06,442 --> 00:17:09,445
OKAY, I AM GOING BACK IN.

425
00:17:09,445 --> 00:17:10,613
( growling )

426
00:17:11,990 --> 00:17:14,575
HEY, "RED ROSS," YEAH.

427
00:17:17,662 --> 00:17:18,663
HI.

428
00:17:18,663 --> 00:17:19,622
HI.

429
00:17:24,126 --> 00:17:25,753
WHAT'RE-WHAT'RE, WHAT ARE THESE?

430
00:17:25,753 --> 00:17:29,131
OH, JUST SOME PICTURES
I MADE AND HUNG UP.

431
00:17:29,131 --> 00:17:31,258
THOUGHT THEY'D
BRIGHTEN UP THE PLACE.

432
00:17:31,258 --> 00:17:32,552
THEY DO, DON'T YOU THINK?

433
00:17:34,971 --> 00:17:37,348
( yipes )
NO, NO, DON'T! DON'T!

434
00:17:37,348 --> 00:17:39,308
( yipes )

435
00:17:41,394 --> 00:17:42,979
I KNOW THERE'S NO HOLE THERE.

436
00:17:42,979 --> 00:17:44,731
I JUST REALLY LIKE THAT PICTURE.

437
00:17:47,525 --> 00:17:49,819
OH, MY GOD, LOOK AT THIS!

438
00:17:49,819 --> 00:17:51,487
OKAY, BUT THERE IS 
A WIRE BACK THERE.

439
00:17:51,487 --> 00:17:53,489
THAT SWITCH
IS CONNECTED TO SOMETHING.

440
00:17:53,489 --> 00:17:57,535
I DON'T CARE. THE WIRES
HAVE COME LOOSE IN YOUR HEAD.

441
00:17:57,535 --> 00:17:59,328
I-I JUST THOUGHT
IF I COULD FOLLOW THE WIRE

442
00:17:59,328 --> 00:18:01,121
I COULD FIND OUT WHAT IT DID.

443
00:18:01,121 --> 00:18:02,289
AND DID YOU?

444
00:18:02,289 --> 00:18:04,291
NO.

445
00:18:04,291 --> 00:18:06,711
DISAPPEARS BACK THERE
BEHIND THAT BASEBOARD.

446
00:18:06,711 --> 00:18:09,672
FOR A MINUTE THERE
I THOUGHT IT WENT DOWNSTAIRS...

447
00:18:11,841 --> 00:18:14,427
( gasps )

448
00:18:14,427 --> 00:18:15,511
BUT IT DIDN'T.

449
00:18:17,430 --> 00:18:19,432
SAY "HELLO"
TO MRS. KATRAKAS.

450
00:18:19,432 --> 00:18:22,184
OH, MY GOD.
Mrs. Katrakas:
HELLO, DARLING.

451
00:18:22,184 --> 00:18:23,978
HELLO, MRS. KATRAKAS.

452
00:18:29,567 --> 00:18:31,945
NOW, ARE YOU SURE
YOU DON'T WANT
TO GO SEE A DOCTOR?

453
00:18:31,945 --> 00:18:34,447
AW, NO.
THAT'LL JUST BRING ME DOWN.

454
00:18:34,447 --> 00:18:36,156
THIS WAS GREAT.

455
00:18:36,156 --> 00:18:37,951
I MEAN,
I-I-I WAS GREAT.

456
00:18:37,951 --> 00:18:39,368
THIS WAS
A GREAT DAY.

457
00:18:39,368 --> 00:18:41,829
YOU KNOW WHAT?
I'M BUYING
EVERYONE COFFEE.

458
00:18:41,829 --> 00:18:43,497
WOULD SOMEONE
JUST GRAB MY WALLET?

459
00:18:43,497 --> 00:18:44,707
IT'S IN MY POCKET.
YEAH, SURE.

460
00:18:44,707 --> 00:18:47,543
NO, NOT YOU.

461
00:18:47,543 --> 00:18:49,879
LOOK, YOUR EYE'S
STILL POPPING OUT
A LITTLE THERE.

462
00:18:49,879 --> 00:18:51,129
I'M GOING TO GO
GET SOME ICE.

463
00:18:51,129 --> 00:18:52,381
OOH, ICE, YEAH.

464
00:18:52,381 --> 00:18:53,674
I'M SO
IN THE MOOD FOR ICE.

465
00:18:53,674 --> 00:18:54,884
YEAH.

466
00:18:54,884 --> 00:18:56,052
AAH...

467
00:18:56,052 --> 00:18:57,720
YOU WERE AMAZING
OUT THERE.

468
00:18:57,720 --> 00:18:58,721
OH...

469
00:18:58,721 --> 00:19:00,473
I KIND OF WAS, WASN'T I?

470
00:19:00,473 --> 00:19:01,641
OH, MY GOD!

471
00:19:01,641 --> 00:19:05,812
I MADE A MAN
TWICE MY SIZE CRY.

472
00:19:05,812 --> 00:19:08,522
I MEAN, I HAVEN'T
DONE THAT SINCE I WAS FOUR

473
00:19:08,522 --> 00:19:10,900
AND I WASHED MY DAD'S
PORSCHE WITH ROCKS.

474
00:19:12,443 --> 00:19:14,361
YOU REALLY ENJOYED
YOURSELF, DIDN'T YOU?

475
00:19:14,361 --> 00:19:15,989
PLEASE, ARE YOU KIDDING?

476
00:19:15,989 --> 00:19:17,865
I-I HURT THREE HUGE MEN.

477
00:19:17,865 --> 00:19:19,826
I GAVE A GUY
A BLOODY NOSE.

478
00:19:19,826 --> 00:19:23,287
I MEAN, I'M-I'M
NOT PROUD OF IT, BUT...

479
00:19:23,287 --> 00:19:25,748
I REALLY AM. I MEAN...
( chuckles )

480
00:19:25,748 --> 00:19:28,042
AND IT'S ALL
BECAUSE OF YOU.

481
00:19:28,042 --> 00:19:31,629
YEAH. WONDERFUL,
AMAZING YOU.

482
00:19:31,629 --> 00:19:33,297
I THINK YOU'VE GOT
A CONCUSSION.

483
00:19:33,297 --> 00:19:34,674
NO. NO, I'M SERIOUS.

484
00:19:34,674 --> 00:19:35,633
THANK YOU.

485
00:19:37,010 --> 00:19:38,928
YOU'RE WELCOME.

486
00:19:38,928 --> 00:19:40,429
( squeals )

487
00:19:40,429 --> 00:19:42,974
I'M SORRY.
DID THAT HURT YOU?

488
00:19:42,974 --> 00:19:44,266
IT'S WORTH THE PAIN.

489
00:19:44,266 --> 00:19:45,685
( chuckles )

490
00:19:45,685 --> 00:19:46,686
YOU KNOW WHAT?

491
00:19:46,686 --> 00:19:48,187
YOU KNOW WHAT?
IT'S NOT.

492
00:19:48,187 --> 00:19:49,313
SORRY.

493
00:19:53,776 --> 00:19:57,363
Announcer:
This is the final boarding call
for flight 664 to Yemen.

494
00:20:00,616 --> 00:20:02,576
WELL, I GUESS
I GOT TO GO.

495
00:20:02,576 --> 00:20:04,954
OH, MY BING-A-LING.

496
00:20:07,623 --> 00:20:09,876
I'LL WAIT FOR YOU.
DO YOU EVEN KNOW

497
00:20:09,876 --> 00:20:12,170
HOW LONG YOU'RE
GOING TO BE GONE?

498
00:20:12,170 --> 00:20:17,675
WELL, JUST UNTIL
WE FIND AN ENERGY SOURCE
TO REPLACE FUEL.

499
00:20:17,675 --> 00:20:21,261
OH. WELL, I'LL
WRITE YOU EVERY DAY.

500
00:20:21,261 --> 00:20:25,183
OKAY.
15 YEMEN ROAD, YEMEN.

501
00:20:26,809 --> 00:20:29,103
OKAY, GOOD-BYE.

502
00:20:29,103 --> 00:20:30,063
GOOD-BYE.

503
00:20:43,659 --> 00:20:44,827
CHANDLER?

504
00:20:44,827 --> 00:20:45,828
NOPE.

505
00:20:45,828 --> 00:20:47,329
CHANDLER!

506
00:20:47,329 --> 00:20:49,707
JANICE, THERE YOU
ARE. THERE YOU ARE.

507
00:20:49,707 --> 00:20:51,250
I HAD TO HAVE
ONE LAST KISS

508
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:53,293
AND ALSO, YOU SAID YOU
WERE GOING TO LEAVE

509
00:20:53,293 --> 00:20:55,379
RIGHT AFTER I GOT
ON THE PLANE.

510
00:20:55,379 --> 00:20:59,050
NO, NO. I-I WANT
TO SEE YOU TAKE OFF.

511
00:20:59,050 --> 00:21:01,343
WELL, THEN I GUESS
I'M GOING TO YEMEN.

512
00:21:03,930 --> 00:21:05,598
I'M GOING TO YEMEN.

513
00:21:07,349 --> 00:21:10,186
WHEN WE GET TO YEMEN
CAN I STAY WITH YOU?

514
00:21:17,985 --> 00:21:21,030
ALL RIGHT. THE SUPER
COULDN'T FIGURE OUT WHAT IT DID.

515
00:21:21,030 --> 00:21:25,159
THE $200-AN-HOUR ELECTRICIAN
COULDN'T FIGURE OUT WHAT IT DID.

516
00:21:25,159 --> 00:21:27,954
I'VE HAD SEVEN
PRETTY SERIOUS SHOCKS.

517
00:21:28,996 --> 00:21:30,414
I OFFICIALLY GIVE UP.

518
00:21:30,414 --> 00:21:32,499
THANK GOD.

519
00:21:32,499 --> 00:21:34,961
GUESS JOEY WAS RIGHT.

520
00:21:36,003 --> 00:21:37,880
IT DOES NOTHING.

521
00:21:42,760 --> 00:21:44,053
SEE?

522
00:21:48,182 --> 00:21:49,433
I'M DOING IT.

523
00:21:49,433 --> 00:21:52,019
I AM TOTALLY DOING IT.

524
00:21:58,818 --> 00:22:00,527
I LOST IT.

